  "prefLabel": "Env-Dw 712.19 Monitoring for Acrylamide and Epichlorohydrin",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Dw 712.19 Monitoring for Acrylamide and Epichlorohydrin. Each O/O shall certify annually in writing to the department that when acrylamide and epichlorohydrin are used in drinking water systems, the combination of dose and monomer level does not exceed the levels specified in Env-Dw 705.05.\n\nSource. #9700, eff 5-1-10; ss by #12668, eff 1-1-19 (formerly Env-Dw 712.18)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-dw700.html"
